From: Johann Hartmann <johann@mayflower.de>
Subject: [PATCH] mm/mmu_notifier: probe mmap_lock only when insertion may register

mmu_interval_notifier_insert() can be called with mmap_lock held for read
after the caller has initialized the interval notifier subscriptions under
the write lock. NVIDIA UVM uses this pattern when creating HMM VA blocks.

The unconditional might_lock() models a possible mmap write-lock acquisition
even when the subscription tree already exists and no such acquisition can
occur. With PROVE_LOCKING, a real read-lock holder gets a recursive-locking
warning and further Lockdep validation is disabled.

Keep the check on the path that calls mmu_notifier_register(), where that
function can acquire mmap_lock. The existing smp_load_acquire and registration
decision remain unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Johann Hartmann <johann@mayflower.de>
---
 mm/mmu_notifier.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mm/mmu_notifier.c
+++ b/mm/mmu_notifier.c
@@ -1024,10 +1024,11 @@ int mmu_interval_notifier_insert(struct mmu_interval_notifier *interval_sub,
 	int ret;
 
 	WARN_ON_ONCE(ops->invalidate_start && !ops->invalidate_finish);
-	might_lock(&mm->mmap_lock);
 
 	subscriptions = smp_load_acquire(&mm->notifier_subscriptions);
 	if (!subscriptions || !subscriptions->has_itree) {
+		/* Registration below may acquire mmap_lock for write. */
+		might_lock(&mm->mmap_lock);
 		ret = mmu_notifier_register(NULL, mm);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
